Phoenix-RTOS: make SDL_SYS_SetThreadPriority() a no-op.

libphoenix's <pthread.h> declares pthread_getschedparam()/
pthread_setschedparam() but does not yet implement them, so the stock pthread
backend link-fails with "undefined reference to pthread_{get,set}schedparam".
Following the pattern SDL already uses for platforms without POSIX thread
scheduling (NACL/RISCOS/OS2), make the call a no-op on Phoenix. Thread
priorities on Phoenix are selected at beginthreadex() time; if per-thread
reprioritization is later needed, implement the two functions in libphoenix
and drop this hunk.

--- a/src/thread/pthread/SDL_systhread.c	2025-01-01 16:48:45.000000000 +0100
+++ b/src/thread/pthread/SDL_systhread.c	2026-08-04 22:51:29.490919499 +0200
@@ -188,8 +188,11 @@
 
 int SDL_SYS_SetThreadPriority(SDL_ThreadPriority priority)
 {
-#if defined(__NACL__) || defined(__RISCOS__) || defined(__OS2__)
-    /* FIXME: Setting thread priority does not seem to be supported in NACL */
+#if defined(__NACL__) || defined(__RISCOS__) || defined(__OS2__) || defined(__phoenix__)
+    /* FIXME: Setting thread priority does not seem to be supported in NACL.
+     * Phoenix-RTOS: libphoenix declares pthread_{get,set}schedparam() but does
+     * not implement them yet, so treat SetThreadPriority as a no-op for now.
+     * (Phoenix thread priority is chosen at beginthreadex() time.) */
     return 0;
 #else
     struct sched_param sched;
